Language English
Debug Off

Book BenBefore Random No Keep Looped
	Triggered By @BenBefore

	Prolog
		Text """
			Benjamin is digging around in his pockets. You think you hear him
			mutter something about a key.
		"""
	End Prolog

	Page HowLong
		Button "<<How long will it take us to look through the house?>>"
		
		Text """
			<<How long, you ask? Well, the house is large. There are numerous
			rooms on the ground floor, a basement, and many rooms upstairs.
			Elize lived here with his son and daughter. The wife died under suspicious
			circumstances when the girl was three. Never explained.>>
			
			Gain 1 {clue}.
			
			<<Anyway, I guess you'll need a few hours just to look through the
			place and get your bearings. You'll want to check every drawer,
			cabinet, and box in the house--take as much time as you need. The
			whole house should be cleared out and spotless by the end of next
			week.>>
		"""

		If Not exploredBackyardNicely Text """
			<<Long enough,>> he snaps. <<There are numerous rooms on the ground
			floor, there is a basement, and there are many rooms upstairs. The
			place has always been too big for the family. Elias lived here with
			his son and daughter. His wife died under suspicious circumstances when the
			girl was three. Never explained.
		
			<<Anyway, you will take whatever time is necessary to look in every
			drawer, cabinet, and box in the house. You are thorough, aren't you?
			And you won't break anything else?>> <<I hope not,>> he mutters
			under his breath.
		"""

		Epilog """
			As he digs through his pockets, he is grumbling something about the
			size of the house and you catch the word... <<indolent>>?
		"""
		
		talkedToBenHowLong = true
		talkedToBenCount = talkedToBenCount + 1
		Trigger @TalkedToBackyardBen
		If talkedToBenCount >= 2 Then Exit
	End Page HowLong

	Page What
		Button "<<What do you think happened to those children?>>"
		
		Text """
			<<The children? One of them was burned from head-to-toe.
			The other two were strangled and parts were... taken. The burns
			were never explained. Nasty business.
		
			<<Elias Smythe--the
			girl's father and the owner of this house--went missing that
			night. Most folks think he did something to the children and
			then ran away. Still hiding, they think.
		
			<<His brother, Peter, also disappeared that night. Folks in
			town figured they'd run off together to avoid difficult questions.>>
		
			Gain 1 {clue}.
		"""

		If Not exploredBackyardNicely Text """
			<<The children? Two were strangled. Parts of them were... missing.
			The burns on the third were never explained. Nasty business.
			
			<<Elias and his brother Peter both went missing that night. Left a
			lot of folks around town wondering what really happened. But we're
			not here to gossip.>>
		"""
		
		Epilog """
			Benjamin is still digging through his pockets. You hear him mutter
			about paying attention and minding your own business.
		"""
		
		talkedToBenChildren = true 
		talkedToBenCount = talkedToBenCount + 1
		Trigger @TalkedToBackyardBen
		If talkedToBenCount >= 2 Then Exit
	End Page What

	Page Where
		Button "<<Where were those children found?>>"
		
		Text """
			<<The children were found just over there,>> he says, pointing back
			the way	you came. <<They were in a pile; the girl's body was still
			smoking from the burns. Strangest thing: she kept smoking until the
			next day. Coroner wasn't able to explain it. No one was.
		
			<<Their family has lived here for generations--many of them in this
			house. They're upset to let it go, but no one lives here... or wants
			to after what happened.>>
		
			Gain 1 {clue}.
		
			Benjamin resumes searching his pockets, but seems a little shaken.
		"""
		
		If Not exploredBackyardNicely Text """
			<<The children were found just over there,>> he grumbles, pointing
			back the way you came. <<Not sure why it matters, but I'll tell
			you:  the girl who was burnt, she kept smoldering until the next
			day. Coroner couldn't explain it.>> Benjamin resumes digging
			through his pockets, but seems a little shaken.
		"""
		
		Epilog """
			Benjamin is still looking through his pockets, but he's moving
			slower and looks upset. You wonder if he's connected is to those
			children.
		"""
		
		talkedToBenWhere = true
		talkedToBenCount = talkedToBenCount + 1
		Trigger @TalkedToBackyardBen
		If talkedToBenCount >= 2 Then Exit
	End Page Where

	Page Why
		Button "<<Why did you wait so long to sell the house?>>"
		
		Text """
			<<Well, they tried right after the... trouble. No one would even come
			to look at it back then, but our, um, priest, told us now is the
			right time.>>
		
			Gain 1 {clue}.
		"""
		
		If Not exploredBackyardNicely Text """
			<<That's none of your concern,>> he snaps.
			
			You startle at his abrupt response. You and all investigators in
			your space suffer 1 facedown horror ({will} negates).
		"""
		
		Epilog """
			Benjamin is looking around on the ground like maybe he dropped
			whatever he's looking for. <i>Could it be a book instead of a
			key?</i> you wonder to yourself.
		"""
		
		talkedToBenWhy = true
		talkedToBenCount = talkedToBenCount + 1
		Trigger @TalkedToBackyardBen		
		If talkedToBenCount >= 2 Then Exit
	End Page Why
	
	Page Sorry
		Not Visible When exploredBackyardNicely

		Button "<<I'm sorry about the gate.>>"
		
		Text """
			<<You should be more careful. The house is old and in poor repair.>>
			His shoulders rise for a moment, then fall as he sighs. <<No real
			harm done... the gate can be repaired... again.>>
		"""
		
		Epilog """
			Benjamin still doesn't look happy, but he doesn't seem as angry now.
		"""
		
		exploredBackyardNicely = true
	End Page Sorry
End Book BenBefore
